  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "A yield aggregator is a decentralised-finance protocol that automatically routes deposited assets across multiple yield-bearing strategies \u2014 such as lending markets, liquidity pools, and staking \u2014 to maximise returns while compounding rewards on the user's behalf. By pooling capital and automating strategy selection, reward harvesting, and reinvestment, aggregators reduce gas costs and operational complexity for individual depositors. Modern aggregators frequently expose tokenised vault shares conforming to standards such as ERC-4626, making positions composable with the wider DeFi ecosystem.",
